/****NEW AUXILIARY SECT CHUNK SUPPORT:
/HIGH 4 BITS OF QUAL WORD ARE NO LONGER USED
/LSDNUM IS ALL ALONE
/IN SECTS, WORD 6 OF SYMBOL TABLE ENTRY (SYMSCT) IS A 15-BIT POINTER
/TO AN AUXILIARY CHUNK.  THE FORMAT OF THIS AUXILIARY CHUNK IS AS FOLLOWS:
/
/0	0 (INDICATES NO SUBSEQUENT CHUNK)
/1	RT (RESTRICTION TYPE) OR FIELD (IF ABSOLUTE)
/2	RESTR (ORIGIN IF ASECT)
/3	LVL/OVR
/4	CONCAT (=1)
/5	LENGTH OF SECT WITHOUT LITERALS (FSECTS ONLY)
/
/WE RECALCULATE THE HIGHEST SECT PC FOR CURRENT SECT
/ON ANY OF THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS:
/
/	PAGE
/	FIELD (*)
/	END-OF-PROGRAM (*)
/	SECT (*)
/	ORIGIN
/
/ (*) WRITE IT OUT
/
/
/NOTE: RESTRICTION BITS:
/
/WORD 5: RESTRICTION ITSELF
/
/WORD 6: BITS 4-11:	LSD NUMBER
/	BITS 0-2:	TYPE OF RESTRICTION
/			0	NO RESTRICTION
/			1	ABSOLUTE FIELD RESTR GIVEN IN WORD 5
/			2	12-BIT ABS ORIGIN RESTR GIVEN IN WD 5
/			3	SAME PAGE & FIELD AS 15-BIT PTR IN WD 5
/			4	SAME FIELD AS 15-BIT PTR IN WORD 5
/
/RT:	RESTRICTION TYPE
	>
